# Patterns are relative to the REPO ROOT: that is the build context.
#
# BuildKit prefers <dockerfile>.dockerignore over <context>/.dockerignore, so
# this is the file it reads for `docker compose build workspace` and for CI.
# VS Code builds from a generated copy of the Dockerfile in its own temp folder
# and reads neither, so keep every COPY in the Dockerfile to a named file.
#
# The image copies the entrypoint and two shell rc files and nothing else, so
# the context is cut down to just this directory. Everything the developer works on arrives at
# runtime through the bind mount, never through the build.

*
!.devcontainer
